# cgm meta API and existing patterns

## Canonical meta reference

- Dev scope inventory: [`Features/Feature_CgmMetaAPI.md`](../../Features/Feature_CgmMetaAPI.md). Implementation source: **`cgm/core/cgm_Meta.py`** — **`cgmNode`** for **non-transform** nodes (shapes, networks, …); **`cgmObject`** is the **transform default** (joints, groups, rig DAG). Shared: `p_nameShort` / `p_nameLong`, messages, `msgList_*`, `getMessageAsMeta`, `connectChildNode`; hierarchy / **`p_parent`** on **`cgmObject`** only.
- When unsure whether a capability exists on meta instances, **read or search that file and nearby callers** instead of assuming Maya-only or ad-hoc patterns.

## Do not add new meta **instance** APIs without approval

**Agents must not** add new **methods on registered `mClass` subclasses** (`cgmDynFK`, `cgmRigBlock`, `cgmObject` subclasses in `mrs/`, `rig/`, etc.) or call **new** `mObj.<method>()` from tools unless the **user explicitly asked** for that meta-class API.

| Default | Instead |
|---------|---------|
| New tool / rig step behavior | **`lib/`** or **`rig/`** **module function** — first arg **`mObj` / `mDynFK` meta** (e.g. **`RIGDYN.chain_set_name(mDynFK, …)`**) |
| User asked for a persistent type method on nodes | Extend the **`mClass`** class **only with approval**; **prompt user to run cgm core reload** (`CGM._reload`) so meta registers in order — **never** partial meta reload inside tool **`reload_dependencies()`** |

Using **existing** meta methods (`p_parent`, `msgList_get`, `msgList_append`, `getMessageAsMeta`, …) is required runtime practice — this rule is about **new** instance methods and **new** calls to methods you just invented. For **ordered scene-linked collections**, prefer **`msgList_*`** over parallel string lists or connection walks — see **`cgm-msglist-patterns`**.

After **module-function** backend edits: tool **Reload Dependencies** + **`reinitializeMetaClass`** re-wrap. After **`mClass` subclass** edits: user **core reload**, then tool reload/rebind. Header “refresh” does not load new Python from disk.

Detail: [`Features/Feature_CgmMetaAPI.md`](../../Features/Feature_CgmMetaAPI.md) § Session reload and agent policy.

## Do not invent lookups that already exist

**Before** any new `def` that uses `mc.ls`, `listConnections`, `listAttr`, `keyframe`, or name-string hacks: **Read** [`Features/Feature_CoreLibLookups.md`](../../Features/Feature_CoreLibLookups.md) and call those names.

Do not add a wrapper whose only job is that query. A new lib function is allowed only after a search shows a real gap — not a type-check or log line on top of an existing call.

## Prefer the codebase over one-off code

- **Before** adding new helpers (extra `mc.ls`, string hacks, duplicate logic), **search the cgmToolsPy3 tree** for existing utilities, meta APIs, or the same problem already solved elsewhere.
- Reuse or extend what is already there unless there is a clear gap and a deliberate reason to diverge.

## Module placement (non-meta code)

- General new utilities belong under **`cgm/core/lib/`**, not vendored trees or unrelated large modules — see **`cgm-module-placement`** rule.

## Runtime: meta handles (mandatory)

- Tool and rig **runtime** code must use **`cgmMeta` instances**, not bare DAG strings, for anything that still exists in the scene. Strings belong in **UI labels** and **saved files** only; convert at load/save boundaries.
- Full rule: **`cgm-runtime-meta-not-strings`**. At **`mc.*`**: **`maya-cmds-strings-only`**.
